# Canonical settings profile for `task velux2mqtt:schema:generate` (cap-0cg, ADR-051).
#
# NOT used at runtime and contains NO real secrets. It exists solely so
# `cosalette schema dump --resolve-settings` can run the configure/expand
# lifecycle and turn the 'cover_device' handler's callable name= NameSpec
# (_cover_map, keyed off settings.covers) into real per-cover channels
# (e.g. blindState/windowState) instead of the generic cover_deviceState
# placeholder. Pin numbers and travel durations are illustrative only —
# they do not need to match any real deployment.
VELUX2MQTT_COVERS=[{"name":"blind","pin_up":17,"pin_stop":27,"pin_down":22,"travel_duration_up":30,"travel_duration_down":28},{"name":"window","pin_up":5,"pin_stop":6,"pin_down":13,"travel_duration_up":20,"travel_duration_down":18}]
